1. d4 d6 {... etc. "F. C. Bryan (Oxford) v. E. E. Ede (Cambridge) was an inferior game by the Cantab, who replied to 1 d4 with 1...d6, intending probably Capablanca's variation lately played in New York and Havana; but he evidently had not sufficiently grasped the principles of this defence, and came to grief speedily. Mr. Bryan obtained an overwleming attack." Source: The Field, 22 March 1913.} 1-0

